      "refersTo": "shelf-card",
      "description": "Cream product evidence card; preview artwork is intentionally omitted from this isolated sample.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-shelf-card\"><div class=\"ds-shelf-copy\"><small>Android + web</small><h2>JuxTravel</h2><p>Travel discovery, independent stays, and a personal travel Passport.</p><div><a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.hostsphere.juxtravel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Play</a></div></div></article>",
      "css": ".ds-shelf-card{min-width:0;background:var(--journal-paper);color:var(--journal-ink);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;font-family:\"DM Sans\",-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}.ds-shelf-copy{padding:14px}.ds-shelf-copy small{font-size:9px;color:#5a655b}.ds-shelf-copy h2{font-size:17px;margin-top:5px;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-shelf-copy p{font-size:11px;line-height:1.6;margin:8px 0 15px;color:#49574e;min-height:53px}.ds-shelf-copy>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;border-top:1px solid var(--journal-rule);padding-top:12px}.ds-shelf-copy a{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;color:var(--journal-red)}.ds-shelf-copy a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.ds-shelf-copy a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #9780f0;outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Technical tags",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "toolbox-tag",
      "description": "Compact informational tags on a dark technical surface.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-toolbox-tags\"><span>React</span><span>Android</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-toolbox-tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;padding:12px;background:#192b27;font-family:\"DM Sans\",-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}.ds-toolbox-tags span{background:#2d473b;color:#e3ebd1;border-radius:3px;font-size:12px;padding:5px 9px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Destination filters",
      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Pressed filter selects All places, Hills, Cities or Heritage; existing focus styling is retained.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-destination-filters\" aria-label=\"Filter destinations\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">All places</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Hills</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Cities</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Heritage</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-destination-filters{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:20px}.ds-destination-filters button{padding:10px 15px;border:0;border-radius:6px;color:#39513e;background:#d8e2ca;font-family:\"DM Sans\",-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;font-size:11px;min-height:40px;cursor:pointer}.ds-destination-filters button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#263f34;color:#fff9e9}.ds-destination-filters button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #9780f0;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:759px){.ds-destination-filters{gap:5px}.ds-destination-filters button{padding:9px 10px;min-height:44px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Destination contact card",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "destination-contact-card",
      "description": "Upright paper card beneath the hero; photo omitted from isolated snippet so source and licensing remain with the real gallery.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-contact-card\" aria-pressed=\"true\" aria-label=\"View Kashmir photograph\"><span><strong>Kashmir</strong><small>Kashmir</small></span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-contact-card{padding:0;text-align:left;background:#faf7e9;border:0;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden;transition:box-shadow .2s;min-width:0;cursor:pointer;font-family:\"DM Sans\",-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}.ds-contact-card:hover{box-shadow:0 5px 15px #193b2228}.ds-contact-card[aria-pressed=true]{outline:2px solid #3c6347;outline-offset:3px}.ds-contact-card:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #9780f0;outline-offset:4px}.ds-contact-card>span{display:block;padding:11px 12px 13px}.ds-contact-card strong{display:block;font-size:13px;color:#243c34}.ds-contact-card small{display:block;font-size:10px;color:#526249;margin-top:4px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-contact-card{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Official app selection",
      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Selection buttons for the two published Android apps; each resets its three-screen carousel.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-app-selection\" aria-label=\"Choose an Android app\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">JuxTravel</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">ResIQ</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-app-selection{display:flex;gap:7px;margin-top:24px;background:#253e34}.ds-app-selection button{font-family:\"DM Sans\",-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;font-size:12px;padding:9px 13px;border:1px solid #809681;background:transparent;border-radius:6px;color:#e4ecd9;min-height:40px;cursor:pointer}.ds-app-selection button[aria-pressed=true]{color:#213b2c;background:#d8e5c4;border-color:transparent}.ds-app-selection button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #9780f0;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:759px){.ds-app-selection{margin:0}.ds-app-selection button{min-height:44px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Personal Editorial Journal",
    "overview": "The portfolio feels like an open journal on Ethan's MacBook. Warm paper, a restrained coral accent, serif storytelling and handwritten photograph captions make the content personal. The preserved desktop chrome, artwork and controls give visitors a familiar way to explore.\n\nMaterials change with the subject: the About cover uses cream paper, the app shelf uses evergreen, travel uses pale green postcards, and the technical toolbox uses a deeper evergreen workspace. A cinematic login introduces the same curiosity through large type over the existing background artwork. These materials express one personal world while allowing its chapters to feel distinct.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Editorial serif headlines paired with practical sans-serif navigation.",
      "Cream paper, coral actions and evergreen working surfaces.",
      "Supplied photography and existing identity artwork as visual anchors.",
      "Thin rules, restrained card depth and functional desktop chrome.",
      "Responsive compositions that retain the story and keyboard access."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Chapter Color Rule",
        "body": "A chapter's headline, action and selected marker share its accent. Change them together when switching chapters.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Story and Control Rule",
        "body": "Use serif type for storytelling and sans-serif type for controls, product metadata and technical tags.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Material Depth Rule",
        "body": "Retain window depth for the desktop frame; use rules and background materials to organize the journal.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the Apple logo, existing application icons, project logos, supplied photographs and background artwork.",
      "Do retain the functioning desktop controls, accessible keyboard navigation and responsive touch interpretation.",
      "Do pair story accents with their selected markers and destination actions.",
      "Do use thin rules and material contrast to organize editorial content.",
      "Do keep app-store availability and travel entries grounded in supplied or verified content.",
      "Do label illustrative destination photography and preserve its source, creator, license and crop notice.",
      "Do display official app screenshots without cropping them inside the device frame or enlarged viewer."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace, recolor or invent identity assets and photographs.",
      "Don't turn Android development into an implied Google Play release.",
      "Don't invent product metrics or destinations to fill visual space.",
      "Don't remove focus indicators or ignore reduced-motion behavior."
    ]
  }
}
